{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1124648-post-apocalyptic-mage-game","id":1124648,"title":"Post apocalyptic Mage game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-04T00:41:57-07:00","id":1124648,"title":"Post apocalyptic Mage game","content":"Hi everyone, I'm running a Mage game set 100 years after a devastating civil war within the technocracy, this war is waged decades (less than 100 years) in the future after the traditions have been all but wiped out and mysticism and religion are things of the past.<br /> <br /> The players are the apprentices of one of the few former technocrats who survived the war, he has had to adapt and internalize a pseudo mystical paradigm in order to survive as have virtually all of the former technocrats who also survived and were scattered across the earth.<br /> <br /> I'm envisioning a level of technology that varies widely with some regions being almost like late 19th or early 20th cities and other regions being almost mediaeval with a few relics of the 'golden age of the past'.<br /> <br /> The technocrats who survived could not go back to an Order of Reason style of magic as they had no access to the information which would have allowed such a paradigm, the modern technocracy does not like its operatives reading texts on the ancient alchemy of the craftmasons from what I know. As such these technocrats had to look in themselves and find a mystical source of inspiration to make their magic work.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any feedback for some of the issues I might run into or ideas on how to make the most of this setting?<br /> <br /> Any thoughts or ideas I might find useful? I'd like to make this a great chronicle for my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T00:51:36-07:00","id":1124650,"title":"","content":"Im still not to sure how your technocrats work, so why don't they just get behind the modern technology of the day and make it better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T01:44:54-07:00","id":1124658,"title":"","content":"I immediately thought(whether right or wrong), the Brotherhood of Steel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T01:46:04-07:00","id":1124659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1124648-post-apocalyptic-mage-game?p=1124650#post1124650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im still not to sure how your technocrats work, so why don't they just get behind the modern technology of the day and make it better?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair question, so the technocrats who survived what is essentially an end of civilization as we know it scenario quickly find out that much of the enlightened science they understand is hyper paradoxical and that their devices break down and fail quite quickly.<br /> <br /> They strain to find a way to work ES (enlightened science) in this reality as technology becomes more a more vulgar with each passing day.<br /> <br /> Imagine a technocrat who works with computers trying to work with an abacus, or a space marine well versed in energy weapons trying to work a forces effect with a flintlock musket; they just wouldn't believe that working ES with such devices would create results.<br /> <br /> I feel that much of the technocracy's low ranking personnel (which is the group who the majority of survivors are comprised of) wouldn't be able to work with such low tech alternatives as they have been conditioned to utilize certain devices as part of their paradigm; as such, technocratic operatives working with the water wheel and the sun dial wouldn't exactly work for them.<br /> <br /> I'm aware I described a more tech heavy setting above but I'm using these low tech examples for a reason, they clearly illustrate the difficulty which technocrats would have working magic in this setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T02:02:01-07:00","id":1124663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1124648-post-apocalyptic-mage-game?p=1124658#post1124658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I immediately thought(whether right or wrong), the Brotherhood of Steel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have been considering a few pockets of technocratic activity where they've really isolated themselves in a reality zone and those areas might resemble the BOS for sure. <br /> <br /> Then again, I think they'd be more like the village in that show The Prisoner depending on who runs them and what they want","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}